Subject: [PATCH 02140/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE F4
 (capstone .397, UNGATED) -- the verifier scorecard. Headline questions: (1)
 did the oracle-distinct selection moat CLOSE the cross-GENERATOR axis on a
 NON-degenerate ARC-GEN pool (the LAST open axis)? (2) was the missing
 partial-state diffusion scorer built LEAK-FREE, and if so did the EXTERNAL
 verifier IMPROVE generation (beat RFG)? (3) did the efficiency Pareto win
 HARDEN against a well-prompted judge? Aggregate: CROSS-GENERATOR = exp4291
 cross_generator_holds + cross_generator_delta + vote_at_1 + oracle_at_k +
 per_substrate_delta; PARTIAL-STATE = exp4292 partial_state_scorer_built +
 partial_state_leak_free + partial_state_auroc; IN-GENERATION = exp4293
 diffusiongemma_guidance_moat + carnot_minus_rfg_delta (if it ran); EFFICIENCY
 = exp4294 efficiency_pareto_holds + cost_ratio; SELF-LEARNING = exp4295
 online_adaptation_helps (tier-2 fixed); ARC = exp4296 total_levels (>=22?);
 hygiene = exp4299 regression_guard_passed. Emit cross_generator_moat_closes +
 in_generation_moat_holds + efficiency_pareto_hardened + verifier_thesis_state
 (one honest string). SKIP any flagged_adversarial artifact; HONOR
 verifier_is_oracle (a circular/execution-grounded win is NOT a moat). Compute
 the G1-G4 publication gate via publication_gate.py. NO gated_on.

Co-Authored-By: Codex CLI <noreply@openai.com>
